# Roles and Permissions (ticket 09).
# Needs a Tenant Admin access token with an Active Tenant (see http/tenants.http) and an Application the
# Tenant has enabled (see http/enablement-role-templates.http), whose Schema has Invoice with read,
# approve and export.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:9800
@tenantToken = paste-tenant-admin-access-token
@applicationId = paste-application-id
@roleId = paste-role-id
@permissionId = paste-permission-id

### Create a Role for an enabled Application (409 if it isn't enabled, or the name exists ignoring case).
### Permissions are optional; each must use a Schema entry that isn't Deprecated (400 otherwise).
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "applicationId": "{{applicationId}}",
  "name": "Clerk",
  "description": "Reads their own open invoices, never exports",
  "permissions": [
    { "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "conditions": { "ownerId": "${user.id}", "status": { "$in": ["open", "paid"] } } },
    { "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "export", "inverted": true }
  ]
}

### The Tenant's Roles, oldest first (paginated: limit, cursor; optional applicationId)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles?applicationId={{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### One Role with its Permissions (Deprecated ones flagged) and the Application Schema
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Rename or re-describe. Works while the Application is disabled too.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Invoice Clerk" }

### Add an allow Permission with a Condition. Placeholders: ${user.id}, ${membership.id}, ${tenant.id},
### each as a whole value. 409 if the Role already has exactly this Permission.
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "resourceType": "Invoice",
  "action": "approve",
  "conditions": {
    "amount": { "$lte": 1000 },
    "approvers": { "$elemMatch": { "membershipId": "${membership.id}" } },
    "status": { "$in": ["open", "submitted"] }
  }
}

### Add a Deny Rule (always wins over any allow)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "approve", "inverted": true, "conditions": { "ownerId": "${user.id}" } }

### Rejected (400): $regex is not allowed in Conditions
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "conditions": { "name": { "$regex": "^a" } } }

### Rejected (400): unknown operator
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "conditions": { "amount": { "$where": "1" } } }

### Rejected (400): $or, $and, $nor and $not aren't evaluated by CASL, so they would never match
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "inverted": true, "conditions": { "$or": [{ "status": "draft" }, { "archived": true }] } }

### Rejected (400): unknown placeholder (only user, Membership and Tenant IDs)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "read", "conditions": { "ownerEmail": "${user.email}" } }

### Rejected (400): an Action outside the Application Schema (a Deprecated one is refused the same way)
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "resourceType": "Invoice", "action": "delete" }

### Remove a Permission, including one on a Deprecated entry
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}/permissions/{{permissionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Every Permission in the Tenant (paginated; optional applicationId and resourceType)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/permissions?resourceType=Invoice
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### Delete a Role and its Permissions (204)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/tenants/current/roles/{{roleId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}

### The changes in the Tenant's Audit Log
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/audit-events?applicationId={{applicationId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{tenantToken}}
